      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me think about what makes a good incident retrospective and structure it well.\n\nKey sections requested:\n1. Impact\n2. Timeline\n3. Contributing factors\n4. Detection gaps\n5. Remediation\n6. Prevention work\n7. Owner handoff\n\nLet me write this in practical language for engineers and managers. Target 450-550 words.\n\nLet me draft this. I want it to be realistic and specific. A bad cache invalidation rule \u2014 this is a classic scenario where a cache key or TTL rule change causes stale data to be served, or causes a cache stampede, or causes a cascade.\n\nLet me think about a realistic scenario: A team changed the cache invalidation rule to key on a user ID instead of a composite key, which caused cache poisoning where stale pricing data was served, or caused a thundering herd when invalidation happened.\n\nActually, let me make it concrete: A bad cache invalidation rule caused stale data to be served (e.g., pricing or inventory), and simultaneously triggered a cache stampede when the invalidation finally fired, overwhelming the backend.\n\nLet me write a realistic timeline.\n\nLet me aim for the word count. I'll write it out.\n\nFormat: This should be a structured document with headers. Headers and some bullet points are appropriate here since it's a retrospective. I'll keep it concise but complete.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n---\n\n# Incident Retrospective: Production API Outage \u2014 Cache Invalidation Rule\n\n**Incident ID:** INC-2024-0317\n**Severity:** SEV-1\n**Duration:** 22 minutes (14:02\u201314:24 UTC)\n**Service:** Orders API\n\n## Impact\n- Orders API returned 5xx errors for ~22 minutes, affecting checkout for all customers.\n- Peak error rate: 34% of requests failed; ~18,000 failed checkout attempts.\n- Estimated revenue impact: ~$42K in lost transactions.\n- Customer support tickets spiked 3x.\n- No data loss or corruption; all failures were availability, not integrity.\n\n## Timeline\n- 14:02 \u2014 Deploy of PR #4471 (cache key change) merged to main and auto-deployed.\n",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me think about what makes a good incident retrospective and structure it well.\n\nKey sections requested:\n1. Impact\n2. Timeline\n3. Contributing factors\n4. Detection gaps\n5. Remediation\n6. Prevention",
