      "stream_token_id_count": 512,
      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a comparison of two deployment options for a local inference service:\n\n1. **Tensor Parallel (TP) across four GPUs** - a single logical model split across 4 GPUs\n2. **Four independent one-GPU replicas behind a router** - 4 separate model instances, each on one GPU, load-balanced by a router\n\nThey want me to discuss:\n- Latency\n- Throughput\n- PCIe traffic\n- Memory pressure\n- Failure isolation\n- Scheduling\n- Model-loading time\n- When each option is the right choice\n\nLet me think through each dimension carefully and provide a thorough, technically accurate comparison. This is a systems/ML infrastructure question. Let me be rigorous.\n\nLet me set up the context. We have a \"local inference service\" - this suggests something like serving LLMs or other ML models locally, possibly on a machine with 4 GPUs (like an A100/H100 node, or a multi-GPU workstation). The comparison is between:\n\n**Option A: Tensor Parallelism (TP)**\n- One model instance, weights sharded across 4 GPUs\n- Requires collective communication (all-reduce) between GPUs for forward/backward passes\n- Typically requires NVLink or high-bandwidth interconnect (or PCIe with NCCL)\n- Scales the compute for a single model\n\n**Option B: Replicas behind a router**\n- 4 independent copies of the model, each on one GPU\n- A router/load balancer distributes requests across them\n- No inter-GPU communication needed\n- Each GPU is fully independent\n\nLet me go through each dimension.\n\n### Latency\n\n**TP:**\n- For a single request, TP has to do the full forward pass across all 4 GPUs with all-reduce communication steps\n- The latency is dominated by the communication overhead between GPUs (all-reduce)\n- With NVLink, this is fast, but still adds latency\n- For a single request, TP latency \u2248 compute time + communication overhead\n- The communication overhead is roughly proportional to the number of all-reduce steps (which scales with model depth)\n- For small models, communication overhead can dominate\n- For large models, the compute is spread out so communication is a smaller fraction\n\n**Replicas:**\n- For a single request, latency is just the compute time on one GPU\n- No inter-GPU communication\n- BUT: if you have 4 replicas and ",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a comparison of two deployment options for a local inference service:\n\n1. **Tensor Parallel (TP) across four GPUs** - a single logical model split across 4 GPUs\n2. **Four independent one-GPU replicas behind a router** - 4 separate model instances, each on one GPU, load-balanced by a router\n\nThe",
