      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a short technical guide for adding a new benchmark to an existing optimization repo. Let me think about what this involves and structure it well.\n\nKey topics to cover:\n1. Where to put scripts\n2. Where to put data\n3. Where to put notes\n4. Where to put patches\n5. Where to put result summaries\n6. How to name run directories\n7. What to record for reproducibility\n8. How to decide whether a result is valid enough to promote\n\nThis is a technical writing task. I should write a concise but complete guide. Let me think about the conventions that are common in optimization research repos (like those for SAT solvers, CP solvers, ILP, etc.).\n\nLet me think about the typical structure of an optimization repo:\n\n- `benchmarks/` or `instances/` - for benchmark instances/data\n- `src/` or `solver/` - the solver code\n- `scripts/` or `tools/` - helper scripts\n- `results/` or `runs/` - run logs and results\n- `notes/` or `docs/` - notes\n- `patches/` - patches\n\nLet me think about naming conventions for run directories. Common patterns:\n- `run_<date>_<hash>` \n- `run_<solver>_<date>`\n- `benchmark_<name>_<date>_<hash>`\n\nFor reproducibility, you need:\n- Exact commit hash / version\n- Hardware specs (CPU, GPU, RAM)\n- Compiler version and flags\n- Environment (Docker image, conda env, pip freeze)\n- Random seeds\n- Input data version\n- Full command line\n- Timing methodology\n\nFor promoting a result:\n- Statistical significance (multiple runs, confidence intervals)\n- Reproducibility (can someone else reproduce?)\n- Sanity checks (known bounds, correctness)\n- Comparison against baseline\n- Documentation\n\nLet me write this as a clean, well-organized guide. I'll use headers and some structure. Keep it \"short\" as requested but complete.\n\nLet me draft this:\n\n---\n\n# Adding a New Benchmark to the Optimization Repo\n\n## Directory layout\n\nI'll propose a layout.\n\n## Scripts\n## Data / instances\n## Notes\n## Patches\n## Result summaries\n## Run directory naming\n## Reproducibility checklist\n## Promotion criteria\n\nLet me write it out properly. I want",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a short technical guide for adding a new benchmark to an existing optimization repo. Let me think about what this involves and structure it well.\n\nKey topics to cover:\n1. Where to put scripts\n2. Where to put data\n3. Where to put notes\n4. Where to put patches\n5. Where to put result summaries\n6. ",
